Tests the engine's collision detection (gc::CollisionSystem).

    collision_test

A world is filled with a few hundred colliders (cubes, spheres and planes, with every kind of transform, some of them children of
a moving parent). Thousands of random ray casts, sphere overlaps and box queries are then compared with slow versions that test
every triangle of every collider in double precision.

This is repeated after colliders are moved, given different meshes, given meshes that don't exist, removed (by deleting the entity
and by removing the component), and after many frames of all of those happening at once, to check that the system keeps up with
the world as it changes. No window is opened. The exit code is zero if every check passed.
